    "updated_at": "2023-09-10T14:08:44Z",
    "body": "Hmm, no, I guess that's not right. \"`Document`'s navigation id\" is meant for WebDriver BiDi, which wants to know about if aborts happen and get signaled, if those aborts happen before DOMContentLoaded. It seems to serve this purpose in the spec just fine, but should probably be renamed.\r\n\r\nThe aborting of the descendants, actually, seems to happen in step 2 of \"abort\":\r\n\r\n> Cancel any instances of the [fetch](https://fetch.spec.whatwg.org/#concept-fetch) algorithm in the context of document, discarding any [tasks](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#concept-task) [queued](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#queue-a-task) for them, and discarding any further data received from the network for them. If this resulted in any instances of the [fetch](https://fetch.spec.whatwg.org/#concept-fetch) algorithm being canceled or any [queued](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#queue-a-task) [tasks](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#concept-task) or any network data getting discarded, then set document's [salvageable](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#concept-document-salvageable) state to false.\r\n\r\nThat will cause the navigations to abort, since they terminate with network errors.\r\n\r\nDoes that make sense? I'll put up a PR renaming \"navigation id\" to help a bit.",
