    "created_at": "2023-09-10T15:10:53Z",
    "updated_at": "2023-09-10T15:10:53Z",
    "body": "> The aborting of the descendants, actually, seems to happen in step 2 of \"abort\":\r\n\r\nRight, canceling fetch is supposed to prevent all subsequent navigation steps from happening. Although, it feels like it still might be the case when an abortion happens after fetching is done and work to run completion steps is scheduled to be executed but hasn't been run yet. Setting ongoing navigation to null will prevent navigation from happening even in this scenario, but just canceling fetch won't. Maybe spec should not be concerned about such cases?\r\n\r\n> Does that make sense? I'll put up a PR renaming \"navigation id\" to help a bit.\r\n\r\nYes, thank you for clarifying this!",
